WEBVTT


00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.660
I recently moved from Korea to Japan and people often ask me

00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:07.880
what's the difference between both

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.500
one of the main thing that comes to my mind

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:16.380
it's the way of things are being handled like in Korea

00:00:16.381 --> 00:00:18.500
it's really the palipali culture

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:22.040
whereas in Japan things takes more times

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.420
so more delicate

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:29.520
so if you get something like even like for the restaurant service

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.260
it's gonna be more delicate

00:00:31.261 --> 00:00:35.780
they gonna do it really properly where in Korea it's gonna be in fast

00:00:35.781 --> 00:00:40.060
fast and you gonna feel comfortable so it depends like the experience

00:00:40.061 --> 00:00:44.460
like the person you are what you want to have around you and depending on that

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:46.760
that's maybe one you gonna prefer

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:52.340
I like both for different reasons so Japan administration can be really slow

00:00:52.341 --> 00:00:55.280
but I still like to do a lot of things with papers

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.620
but there's also this thing where it keeps an authenticity

00:00:59.621 --> 00:01:06.300
like it keeps also some old style old ways and it's mixing with like

00:01:06.301 --> 00:01:09.380
modernity I really like that way uh

00:01:09.381 --> 00:01:13.100
in Korea it is true everything is fast that's really convenient

00:01:13.101 --> 00:01:15.400
really convenient nothing to say on that

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.980
then following this like the dynamic is really like different

00:01:19.981 --> 00:01:25.680
like I I had an example in a work where in Korea people will scream

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.160
where in Japan I felt more respected

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.640
uh as a human is it you just talk,

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:37.560
just talk you do and you try to understand each other 

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.100
but like You have also in friendship

00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:42.820
you can be maybe more loud in Korea,

00:01:42.821 --> 00:01:46.060
of course, there is different settings like don't do it randomly,

00:01:46.061 --> 00:01:48.860
but feels like you can be a bit more expressive.

00:01:48.861 --> 00:01:51.580
And of course, like in Japan,

00:01:51.581 --> 00:01:53.900
like people really like

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.840
taken under consideration of the people

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.740
so they're not gonna be a disturbance to others. Um,

00:02:01.741 --> 00:02:05.420
but of course then it's also some pressure for,

00:02:05.421 --> 00:02:09.580
for them to not be too loud and things like that.

00:02:09.581 --> 00:02:10.740
So of course, like,

00:02:10.741 --> 00:02:12.180
you know, that's good and bad,

00:02:12.181 --> 00:02:17.800
but I think it's all connected to the way they kind of behaved and both,

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.200
both are really respectful.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.600
It's just the way they express themselves that are different.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.700
So I think another way to say it is like

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:31.120
Korea feels really comfortable for many reasons

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:38.720
and Japan feels like fresh hair with

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.800
beauty in every details.
